{'type': 'text', 'text': '### Executive Incident Summary\n**Event Identifier:** EVT-00030  \n**Classification:** DoS Hulk (HTTP Denial of Service Flood Attack)  \n**Severity:** High / Critical (Volumetric Denial-of-Service Traffic)  \n**Time Range:** 2017-05-07 10:49:00 UTC – 2017-05-07 10:50:00 UTC (Duration: 60s)\n\n---\n\n### Key Findings & Technical Details\n\n1. **Network Activity & Targets:**\n   - **Source IP:** `172.16.0.1`\n   - **Destination IP:** `192.168.10.50` (Target HTTP Web Server)\n   - **Target Port:** Port `80` (HTTP) across a broad distribution of ephemeral client source ports (e.g., 36184, 43222, 54524, 59624, 59626).\n   - **Protocol:** TCP (IP Protocol 6)\n\n2. **Traffic & Flow Statistics:**\n   - **Flow Volume:** 5,000 flows logged in metadata; 34,533 matching flow records identified within the active event window.\n   - **Anomaly Scores:** Mean event anomaly score of `-0.1331` (individual flow scores reaching down to `-0.2030`, indicating highly abnormal traffic patterns).\n   - **Behavioral Indicators:** High-frequency generation of HTTP requests with TCP FIN flag terminations and high flow durations, characteristic of the **Hulk** DoS tool targeting resource exhaustion on web services.\n\n3. **Attack Chain & Campaign Context:**\n   - **Temporal Propagation:** `EVT-00030` is part of a continuous, multi-minute DoS campaign originating from `172.16.0.1` towards `192.168.10.50`.\n   - **Predecessor & Successor Events:** Directly preceded by `EVT-00028` and `EVT-00029` (10:48:00 – 10:49:00 UTC) and succeeded by `EVT-00031` and `EVT-00032` (10:50:00 – 10:51:00 UTC).\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Remediation Steps\n1. **Immediate Mitigation:** Implement rate-limiting or automated IP blocking rules on firewall/WAF for host `172.16.0.1` targeting port 80.\n2. **Server Inspection:** Assess web server responsiveness and resource consumption on `192.168.10.50` during the attack window.\n3. **Upstream Rule Enforcement:** Apply Web Application Firewall (WAF) mitigation rules to filter randomized, high-volume HTTP request floods.', 'extras': {'signature': ''}}